        "code": "import json\n\ntry:\n    document = json.loads(payload)\nexcept ValueError as error:\n    return {\"collections\": [],\n            \"errors\": [\"collections response is not JSON: %s\" % error]}\n\nif isinstance(document, dict):\n    listed = document.get(\"collections\")\nelif isinstance(document, list):\n    listed = document\nelse:\n    listed = None\nif not isinstance(listed, list):\n    return {\"collections\": [],\n            \"errors\": [\"no collection list in the response\"]}\n\nout = []\nfor entry in listed:\n    if not isinstance(entry, dict) or not entry.get(\"id\"):\n        continue\n    out.append({\n        \"id\": str(entry[\"id\"])[:200],\n        \"title\": str(entry.get(\"title\") or entry[\"id\"])[:300],\n        \"description\": str(entry.get(\"description\") or \"\")[:2000],\n        \"can_read\": bool(entry.get(\"can_read\", True)),\n        \"can_write\": bool(entry.get(\"can_write\", False)),\n        \"media_types\": [str(m) for m in (entry.get(\"media_types\") or [])],\n    })\nreturn {\"collections\": out, \"errors\": []}",
        "doc": "Read a TAXII collections response.\n\nA missing `can_read` is taken as readable. TAXII 2.0 servers routinely omit\nit, and refusing to poll a collection the server would happily have served\nis a worse failure than trying and being told no.",
